            "review_title": "Review at Shifu Dimsum 175 de Tham",
            "review_text": "Nostratamis\nTraralgon, Australia246 contributions\n0\nFood Ok, but much better value around\nAug 2014 • Solo\nThis place is new and looks attractive and, ok, offers nice dim sum.\nBUT... beware their menu prices have 10% added to the bill at the end, when all other restaurants show tax inclusive prices on their menus. No big deal? Maybe not but irritating.\nAlso... a refresher towel is provided when you take your seat which is fairly standard around here.\nDifference is, this place charges it to your bill (plus 10%) and most others don't. Again, no big deal but not expected.\nThere is great value to be had when eating in this area of HCM and one can eat very well on a tight budget.\nIn my estimation, if you were to eat a substantial meal at Shifu, the cost to do so would make it the most expensive restaurant in the area. By far!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 29, 2014",
